# What comes out of the dark.
#
# There are no turns here, so there are no `move` blocks and no intents: an enemy's whole
# behaviour is its own `on every <n>s:` listeners, pumped by the clock. That is the single
# largest difference between writing a real-time enemy and a turn-based one, and FINDINGS #2
# and #3 are about what it costs.
#
# None of them places itself. Spawning an enemy raises no event at all -- `created` is for
# `create`, `copy` and `shuffle` -- so there is nothing in content for a listener to hang on,
# and a wave that walks in from the back rank has to be put there by whoever spawned it. The
# host does it with `Execute("self.rank = 3", id, 0)` and every test below does it by hand.
# FINDINGS #5.
#
# `random party` rather than `player`: `player` is the leader alone, and an enemy that always
# swings at the leader is the bug CT326 exists to stop. CT326 does not look inside a listener,
# so nothing would have told me. FINDINGS #6.

# The common one. Closes a rank every two seconds; once it is on the line it swings instead.
enemy "Hollow"
  hp 16
  on every 2s:
    if not self.has(Reeling):
      if self.rank > 0:
        self.rank -1
      else:
        deal 5 to random party

# Never closes. Stands where it arrived and throws, which is what makes `range` matter: a keeper
# who spends everything on what is nearest never reaches the Wisps and loses slowly.
enemy "Wisp"
  hp 10
  on every 3s:
    deal 3 to random party

# Slow and heavy, and angrier once it is hurt. A phase gates a `move`, and there are no moves
# here, so the halfway change is a filter on a second listener instead.
enemy "Breaker"
  hp 40
  on every 3s:
    if self.rank > 0:
      self.rank -1
    else:
      deal 9 to random party
  on every 3s (self.hp <= self.max_hp / 2):
    deal 4 to random party

# The thing the keepers are holding against, and a workaround for the hardest finding of the
# round: a battle is over the moment no enemy is left standing, so in a game where waves arrive
# on a timer the fight ends in the gap between two of them. The Dark is an enemy that is always
# there and can never be pointed at, so the board is never empty and the hold runs on the clock
# instead of on the body count. It stands on rank 4, which no wave ever walks to. FINDINGS #7.
enemy "The Dark"
  hp 9999
  modify targetable: set 0
